# fallout_le 0.82 - Spike 3 (64-bit ARM): drafted by s3port.py (PAD-1287) from the Spike 3 port star_wars_elg-1.10.port (star_wars_elg 1.10).
# Functions paired across the two titles: 9771 of 18297 reference functions (8213 anchored by vtable slots and strings, 377 through calls that line up, the rest grown through calls); half of them line up 100% or better.
# Written: what the reference port carries that is the FRAMEWORK's (each site's function at least 75% alike its
# reference's, each global and offset read at the lined-up instruction, the engines' layouts re-read off this program's
# own code); the switch lines from this program's own device table. The reference game's own content (shows, lamps,
# callouts, scenes, held coils, its modes) is not this title's: written as comments, for its own port.
# Emulator-proven 2026-11-15 (PAD-1288) on the Spike 3 rig (s3proof.sh PROOF=mode TITLE=fallout_le, slot 63, hidden,
# muted; prebuilt/mode64.so): the runtime took this port (29 sites, 39 shots), held back the Insider achievement query
# (type 28), armed the 6 events with the dispatch hooked and both switch_hit sites; in play CLOCK TEST started on the
# third Junk target hit (switch 38), scored 6 shots on Pop target-left / Radio tower target / 3 Bank-top through the
# game's score_add (+21,000,000: 11,970 -> 21,596,280) and ended when its 25 s ran out, the game playing on to the
# 380 s cap; run twice, the same. Program sha1 19081048c0b2427efca8c05775efb109e13689da (games/game).
# Ball save emulator-proven 2026-11-15 (PAD-1288, slot 64): a mode's 15 s save taken (the game is saving), the drain
# inside it served back (trough eject, auto plunger, 1 s later), 3 shots scored +6,000,000 on that ball, and the drain
# after the save ended the mode with the ball; the control with no save (slot 65) ended on its first drain, 5.9 s in.
# Multiball emulator-proven 2026-11-15 (PAD-1288, slot 66): `multiball 3 10` through the game's serve, 2 more balls
# ejected to 3 in play, 3 shots (+6,000,000), its 40 s clock, drains 3 -> 2 -> 1 and the multiball handed back.
# Switch edges (PAD-1322's 64-bit source, carried at the merge with main) emulator-proven 2026-11-15 (PAD-1288,
# slots 63/64, this build's mode64.so): switch_edge 0x71b8b4 hooked in the drain's loop; with it the clock run above gave
# the same result (6 shots, +21,000,000, ended on its 25 s clock); PROOF=edge with `value switch_edge_log 400` logged the
# flipper buttons (24, 25) in attract, the Right slingshot (23, no handler bits) and every Junk target hit in play.
# Not carried: the game's own mode flags (Star Wars ELG's mode books), held coils (no coil_take counterpart), lamps,
# shows, screens and clips - this title's own work.

game           fallout_le
version        0.82

